Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:42:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: wait for the panorama grid to really stop and learn
 browse shapes ahead

Two gaps let a learnt shape flip a cell in front of the user, and the
browse page learnt every shape only once the cell was already on screen.

* Settling: the grid counted as settled whenever isScrollInProgress was
  false. Dragging the fast-scroll thumb is a run of short scrollToItem
  calls with false in between, so shapes landed mid-drag; the same
  happened in the pause between two flings. rememberPanoramaGridSettled
  now reports settled only after 300 ms without scrolling.
* Browse prefetch: PrefetchPanoramaCoverShapes requests the covers of
  entries that are loaded but not on screen yet (paging loads the next
  page ahead of the user) at 128 px, inexact, without the memory cache,
  and records their shapes. The download lands in the disk cache the
  cell reads afterwards. Requests are disposed when the grid leaves.

PanoramaCoverShapes.kt stays byte-identical between mihon-harmony and
anikku-harmony.

Same change as mihon-harmony 0019. Anikku also uses the debounced
settle in the related-entries grids; they get no prefetch (short lists).
